    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n47769" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tĕnellus</span></b> , a, um, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>adj. dim.</i>
			[tener], <i>somewhat tender</i> or <i>delicate</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">bella et tenella Casina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Cas. 1, 20</span></i>
			: vates, Domit. Mart. poët. ap. <i><span class="en">Suet. Gram.
			16</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ungulae pullorum equinorum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 2, 7, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vultus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					S. 5, 5, 86</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tenellum enim cito facit putre (aqua),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 41, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
